family: set-cli
what: poll
transport: v2c
address: logs-01.example.net
verification: reference
reference: common set-style SNMP statements (set snmp community …, set snmp v3 …); RFC 3414 (USM) and RFC 3415 (VACM)
does: Lets Woodshed poll the device's SNMP agent (SNMPv2c, read-only, from Woodshed's address only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with the device's name and interfaces; after the first cycle the device page shows its graphs.
placeholders: <COMMUNITY> <WOODSHED-IP>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- A client list takes addresses, not names: <WOODSHED-IP> is the address Woodshed polls from (logs-01.example.net resolves to it), /128 for IPv6.
- Then add the device in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, SNMPv2c and the same community.
---- part cli "": Enter in configuration mode, then commit
set snmp community <COMMUNITY> authorization read-only
set snmp community <COMMUNITY> clients <WOODSHED-IP>/32
commit
==== text
